<!-- CONCLUSION -->

<section>

  <h2 class="section-title">
    Conclusion
  </h2>


  <div class="card">

    <p>
      The Stirling engine experiment demonstrated a clear relationship
      between thermal gradient and mechanical output. As the temperature
      difference increased, flywheel speed increased approximately
      linearly.
    </p>

    <br>

    <p>
      The measured data produced a regression of RPM = 3.26(ΔT) − 10.8,
      corresponding to an estimated startup temperature difference of
      approximately 3.3°C. The ice trial further demonstrated that
      reversing the thermal gradient reverses the direction of rotation.
